{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "025J", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-functorial-etale}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3057e826b9ddc3475601fb13037ff53c7e67ec62dcf1a6356c939b9d318d1df2", "source_text": "The functorial characterization", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1b9b4b04ac73d994e696eb03068ea7b9b494c106a0afa5fb10447b3e4c99cc8a", "unit_id": "tag:025J:title"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "025J", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$0$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3fa23b0b63474bb791fe77aa109d46b4825e3d9a88d0b113ae1aff7badeef846", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:997f5bfbce1501c399e50699ce3679fb4564048d09c786d98032b8f111eeba80", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe finally present the promised functorial characterization.\nThus there are four ways to think about <ACCENT_0001>tale morphisms of schemes:\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> as a smooth morphism of relative dimension <MATH_0001>,\n<STRUCT_0004> as locally finitely presented, flat, and unramified morphisms,\n<STRUCT_0005> using the structure theorem, and\n<STRUCT_0006> using the functorial characterization.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c2d1e7b5c1be4f2bc7c7c6bdee6aff1ed06f4f19961893f183b9c89d18252aee", "unit_id": "tag:025J:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "025J", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$Y$", "MATH_0005": "$Y_0 \\subset Y$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\Mor_S(Y, X) \\longrightarrow \\Mor_S(Y_0, X)\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-formally-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:27e06a7e12d21395616a9ddd87c3dbce40c1fbb50370b13f7f942a98fb3125ae", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:93186453b4a61c5cf691ab71a871b90a230d57d44a2de001361ff088a2a98601", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism that is locally of finite presentation.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is <ACCENT_0001>tale,\n<STRUCT_0003> for all affine <MATH_0003>-schemes <MATH_0004>, and closed subschemes <MATH_0005>\ndefined by square-zero ideals, the natural map\n<MATH_0006>\nis bijective.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a47f6cba0e6542b6b6d3a4969ebdf7b67198ee492581c2f8dfe18302e93c5758", "unit_id": "tag:025K:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "025J", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-lemma-etale-formally-etale}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2a92d38e029b632112370f8f3ed210097ed3cdafaafe69e41bdfd51514ff4c22", "source_text": "This is\nMore on Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7d7a7e9849696afbcf9a3a67d541c6d9c3a77c933f98b4f61a8c80d3d24c7ca4", "unit_id": "tag:025K:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "025J", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2cdd54c91172842da7935e351b2e537dfc65808da525fec53dd82898c278104", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a755e4677f449b440dc83173ebc65eaa03bcd3055758a7c2703c67219c1ca41b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis characterization says that solutions to the equations defining <MATH_0001> can\nbe lifted uniquely through nilpotent thickenings.\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:adf7bc91ac0a22e4dd78a39ef57bdf6157fd580a2bc210453ba1a2441fc51d90", "unit_id": "tag:025J:prose-0002"}
